WEBVTT

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.050
<i>Hold me tight,</i>

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.050
<i>like the magnificent seas embracing the waves.</i>

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>Take me back to your hidden house</i>

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.850
<i>inside the mountains.</i>

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.270
Yahoo~

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.650
What are you going to do when the first snow falls?

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.980
What about you?

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.910
<i>To the house where the roof is thatched with happiness</i>

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.120
<i>and the door is made of love.</i>

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.630
<i>But what should I do</i>

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:56.510
<i>when first love calls on me again?</i>

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.280
We'll have to discuss Block C later;

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.250
apparently, they're going to use it

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.950
to hold events through the end of the year.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.790
Won't that make the schedule a little too tight?

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.250
It's not like we can do anything about it.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.630
Are you sure there's nothing going on?

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.510
Why do you ask?

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.900
I gave you a two-day vacation and you still look miserable.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:01.800
Are you sick?

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.370
Don't worry.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.510
I got plenty of rest and relaxation.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.810
So that's where you two were.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.810
How about that Christmas atmosphere?

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.360
This is apparently <i>the</i> place for proposals during the winter season.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:20.360
Come again?

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.910
Haven't you heard about it?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.610
I guess that's no surprise.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.870
I bet you've heard of it though, Miss Yujin:

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.750
"Eleven": the fabled place where no proposal can possibly fail.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.960
In this legendary place everyone will say "okay" when proposed to.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.170
That's impossible.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.480
You don't believe me?

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.630
Do you want to bet on it?

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:43.630
Even if I were to propose to you here, you'd definitely say "okay."

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.390
No thanks.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.620
Since it's lunchtime,

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.310
why don't we go grab something to eat?

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.190
That's right. Eating sure is important.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.020
Who cares about proposals and love; it's eating that really counts.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.570
Isn't that Director Lee over there?

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:09.080
The building in Block A's been superannuated, so pay close attention to it.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.660
And then Block B...

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.370
He's supposed to present a construction progress report

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.380
to the main company today.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.050
Was it all right for him to leave the hospital so soon?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.670
I don't really know.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:24.310
He went missing for five days after he left the hospital

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.010
and came back today, after all.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.470
What about Block C?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.140
We'll have to hold off on that area for now.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.600
Would you like to go for a drink after work today?

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.850
Sounds good to me.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.900
You too, Miss Yujin. Okay?

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.980
We'll see.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.410
Where and what have you been doing?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.420
I was looking for someone.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.380
I don't mind that you're looking for someone,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.740
but I'd much prefer that you find

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.420
Director Minhyung Lee before looking for anyone else.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.430
I didn't know why I kept bothering with this,

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.800
but now I think that maybe there are things

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.850
that I want to remember piece-by-piece.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:17.940
I'm such a fool.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:23.400
Oh right, Miss Yujin did say something similar.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.400
Why did you bring that up all of a sudden?

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:32.490
For the past few days, I've been looking everywhere for this one piece,

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.040
but I think perhaps,

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:38.670
if this is a puzzle that can't be fulfilled or completed,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.040
maybe I should give up on it.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:04.020
Hello?

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.280
Oh hi, Sanghyuk.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:06.990
That's tomorrow, huh?

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.030
Don't worry, I'll bring your mother with me.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.170
Okay.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.490
I'm counting on you, Father.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.120
I'm already on my way down, so please be careful on the road.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.790
I'll see you tomorrow then.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.710
Yongguk, it's me.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.510
I need you to do me a favor.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.000
So Chelin told you everything, huh?

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:05.000
Did this Joonsang guy really look like me that much?

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:15.810
The reason why you cried when we first met

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.430
was because I reminded you of him, wasn't it?

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:23.220
Same with why you tried to quit,

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.440
and acted cold towards me,

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.980
and ran out into the snow that night...

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:31.400
It's all because of him, isn't it?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.580
What kind of a person was Joonsang?

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.250
Were you two close?

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:50.920
I'm betting that, other than looking like alike,

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.760
we're two completely different people.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.970
I'm sorry if I kept misleading you.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:02.940
Oh no, I'm actually quite thankful.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.850
I've always wondered

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:08.150
what Joonsang would look like if he were still alive,

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:11.360
since I only knew Joonsang as he was when he was eighteen.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:16.620
I wondered what Joonsang would look like if he were twenty-eight like me.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.160
But...

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:23.960
thanks to you, I was able to meet Joonsang again.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:27.380
A twenty-eight year old Joonsang, that is.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.270
Hey, Joonsang...

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.110
Could you let go of her hand?

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.160
Yujin is my fiancée.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.420
I won't allow any further such rude behavior.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.130
Come on, let's go.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:12.460
Wait.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.140
There's something I want to ask Miss Yujin.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.640
You still haven't forgotten Joonsang, right?

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.600
I thought I warned you.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:25.980
I haven't heard her answer yet.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.860
You still love Joonsang, don't you?

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.360
What did you say?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.360
What did you say?

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.500
Let's go, Yujin.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:12.360
Let's talk, Sanghyuk.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:14.730
Promise me.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.190
Sanghyuk!

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:18.740
Promise me, that even if Joonsang were to come back to life,

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.660
you'd stay by my side.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.480
That's a promise.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.740
You have to keep it, okay?

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.250
I won't ask you to forget about Joonsang.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.460
After all, you're entitled to remember and fantasize all you want.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:42.680
The wedding...

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.430
Could we reconsider it?

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:49.390
What are you saying?

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:54.230
Can't we just go back to being friends?

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:57.940
It's all just too confusing for me; it's too much.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.510
No, we can't.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.910
I'll never let you go.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.200
Sanghyuk...

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:05.780
You just have to be yourself, just like you always were.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.540
I mean, you've never loved me, right?

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.420
Am I wrong?

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:17.550
Have you ever loved me, even for a single moment?

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.430
It doesn't matter.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:25.010
<i>I</i> love you.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.390
That's the concert proposal.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:35.730
I agreed to appear as a guest, so go over the details for me.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:36.520
Yes, Miss.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.030
I thought we already turned this offer down once?

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.350
Don't you think it'd be better for you to appear on TV

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:45.450
if you want to promote your upcoming concert?

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.580
We've already received a few offers.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.770
It's already been a few days since I've seen Minhyung.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.500
Just fit it into my schedule.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:57.250
I've been waiting for you.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.010
Mr. Minhyung.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:04.550
Hey, Joonsang!

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.270
So it <i>was</i> you.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:15.270
How did you go on living without remembering that you were Joonsang?

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.270
What in the world happened?

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:23.360
Did you lose your memories because of the traffic accident or something?

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:27.530
I see.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:29.990
Yeah, that must be it.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.790
What do you want from me?

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.880
You must be here because you want something from me.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.050
Mr. Minhyung,

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:51.010
it doesn't matter to me if you <i>are</i> actually Joonsang.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:56.940
You can't have Yujin, even if you are Joonsang.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.150
This is your last warning.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:07.700
Please don't confuse Yujin any more.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:08.870
Why?

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:10.580
Joonsang...

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:15.870
Isn't Joonsang the one Yujin's been waiting for all this time?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.170
So why?

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.170
You have no right!

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.800
Neither Joonsang nor Minhyung have that right.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.370
Yujin, that stupid girl...

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.930
may actually have liked Joonsang,

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.290
but not you.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.180
You were just using her.

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:36.890
Is that true?

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.940
You said so yourself.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:43.440
You said you used Yujin to get at me.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.940
Am I wrong?

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.300
D-Did I really?

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.620
I don't remember.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.590
Did Joonsang really do that?

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.560
I don't remember.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:06.260
Why did I try to get at you?

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.300
I don't really know,

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:14.890
but you did approach my father and use Yujin, all to get at me.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.310
Did Joonsang really use Miss Yujin?

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:23.480
So they didn't love each other then?

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.650
If you can't remember anything,

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:30.740
then it doesn't really matter, even if you <i>are</i> Joonsang.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.330
Just leave her alone.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.960
Please don't make Yujin suffer any more than she has already.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:47.050
Haven't the last ten years been enough?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:52.970
Isn't it enough for you that you made Yujin suffer for the last ten years?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.470
Please let Yujin go.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.460
<i>The number you are trying to reach is not available at this time.</i>

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:20.790
<i>Please leave a message after the beep.</i>

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.960
I really didn't want to keep saying "sorry,"

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:32.840
but I'm sorry, Sanghyuk.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.010
That's right, I lied.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:39.330
But it's just like Sanghyuk told you:

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.520
Joonsang never liked Yujin.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.190
It was the same for Yujin.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:51.280
She was pretending to like Joonsang because he liked me.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.490
Miss Yujin cried when she saw me for the first time.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:57.730
She kept glaring at me and kept her guard up around me,

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.540
and all the while she tried to avoid me.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:03.120
No one could do that unless they really liked someone.

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.080
So what?

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:09.250
So that's making you hesitate?

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:12.670
I thought you didn't remember anything?!

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.010
Let's stop.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.550
You're right.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.760
Yujin liked Joonsang too.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:23.770
But Joonsang liked <i>me,</i> not Yujin!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.690
There are times when the strings of my heart

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:32.070
become unwound and are released toward someone.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:33.820
Stop.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.360
Even I don't know where the end of that string will reach.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.450
That's enough.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:39.280
But this, I know for sure:

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:44.660
once that string is released, it can't be wound back up again.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.540
Please, I don't want to hear any more.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.000
Chelin...

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.760
Let's talk later.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:55.800
Let's break up.

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:02.310
If that's what you want, I won't object any further.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.310
No, I'll head over there.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.040
Minhyung Lee.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.170
Joonsang Kang.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:02.660
It's really dangerous so hold on tight to me, okay?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:07.580
Did you go over the soundboard settings?

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.870
Yes, it's all ready to go.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.630
How's it all going, Producer Kim?

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.840
That guy over there is Miss Yujin's fiancée, right?

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:19.380
Shall we break for lunch?

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:23.360
He managed to pull a concert together at his fiancée's work site, huh?

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.350
The guy's got some skills.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.410
It's me, Yujin.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.910
Are you sick or something?

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:54.960
Could you say it one more time?

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.000
So there really is no way to do it?

00:18:57.130 --> 00:19:00.010
Were you expecting me to perform some sort of magic trick?

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.430
No, but...

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:08.430
You decided to reject your past memories of your own accord.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:12.440
I have a reason to reclaim those memories now.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.520
There's someone who still remembers Joonsang

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:17.320
and is waiting for him, even now.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:23.240
I only performed hypnosis to try and cure you.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:27.030
But you planted these false memories inside of me.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:30.790
Those false memories were meant to be like bookmarks

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:35.250
on the off chance that you might want to reclaim your memories some day.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:40.590
Now that you've found the bookmark, you need to turn the page over.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:42.340
Is that it?

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:45.930
You'll have to read over the lost pages again, sentence by sentence.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:50.310
If it's as easy as you say it is, why can't I still remember anything?

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.770
Because you've buried these memories for ten years.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.080
I guess I can't reject the possibility

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.320
that you might somehow be able to instantaneously

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.150
recover all your memories,

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:01.990
but there's also the chance that you may never be able to remember them.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:08.310
After all, I was never able to get to the bottom of why you were trying

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:11.000
to cover up your past.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.970
There's no telling what would happen

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:16.500
if you were to recover those memories as well.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.590
You may be better off not remembering.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.580
Yes, Mother.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.520
All right.

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.650
Just leave it. I'll clean up later.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:38.940
Oh, you.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.970
You should be taking medicine or going to the hospital if you're ill,

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:44.200
not laying around sick by yourself.

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:47.490
Thanks, I think I'm better now.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:56.250
Did Sanghyuk say anything?

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.290
About what?

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:01.750
Strange.

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:06.160
He told me to hurry up on the wedding dress

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.220
because he wanted to settle on a date for the wedding.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.390
Sanghyuk said that?

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:14.730
Sanghyuk and I are...

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:19.370
I'm sorry about how I acted back then.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:21.730
Minhyung had collapsed and all;

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.530
I must not have been myself.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:24.970
It's all right.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:26.700
I was the one who was mistaken, after all.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:36.460
Aren't you going to pick up?

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.580
I don't recognize this number.

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:42.170
I better get going.

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:46.050
Minhyung's waiting for me; we're supposed to have dinner together.

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:53.510
Hey, Sanghyuk.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:15.720
I understand why you'd want to recover Joonsang's memories,

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:19.580
but you must not allow the past to destroy who you are now.

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:23.040
For both yourself and your mother.

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:27.510
Call me whenever you need my help.

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:29.760
That goes for you too.

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:33.890
I'll come visit you as soon as I'm back in America.

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:56.540
Aren't you Joonsang Kang?

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:10.840
You used to come to my lectures, remember?

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:12.640
It's me, Jinwoo Kim.

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:14.600
Father.

00:23:16.970 --> 00:23:17.680
You're here.

00:23:17.810 --> 00:23:19.020
Hi, Sanghyuk.
